id: pm-t4d7nz
title: "Outcome milestone: universal domain platform — non-PM systems are buildable on pm SDK primitives alone"
description: ""
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 3
tags[7]: digital-twin,extensibility,"horizon:far",milestone,outcome,sdk,universal-tool
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:44:02.049Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T09:59:02.751Z"
deadline: "2028-06-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 12000
acceptance_criteria: "Custom types, statuses, workflows, fields, and relationship kinds are fully definable at runtime with lossless migration; Principal-based item-level policy is enforced at the SDK layer, not per-surface; Cross-workspace federation supports context, dependencies, and aggregation across many repositories; A published exemplar outside project management ships with an empty SDK gap ledger; Project profiles let a workspace be reshaped for a non-software domain without editing core"
goal: universal-domain-platform
objective: "A developer models a foreign domain — version control, business workflows, a digital twin — using only public pm SDK primitives"
value: "Proves the central product claim: pm is an event-sourced, graph-native context substrate, and project management is one application of it."
impact: Opens the addressable surface beyond software backlogs and turns the extension ecosystem into a platform rather than a plugin list.
outcome: "At least three foreign-domain exemplars ship with no core forks, no private-core imports, and a published gap ledger that is empty."
why_now: The first two exemplars (a git-like VCS and a temporal digital twin) already shipped and produced a gap report; the remaining gaps decide whether the platform claim is real or aspirational.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
