body: "## Outcome\npm SDK primitives — typed items, custom status graphs, a relationship registry, immutable event history, point-in-time reconstruction, transactional multi-item commits, and bounded graph queries — are sufficient to model domains that have nothing to do with software backlogs.\n\n## Evidence already recorded\nTwo exemplars landed and closed: a git-like version-control extension and a temporal digital-twin phase-2 exemplar. Their gap reports named the missing primitives; the transaction waiver has since been retired. This milestone tracks the remaining distance.\n\n## Delivery chain\npm-8jdc schema/config completion (incl. pm-z5nb, pm-dijg migrations) -> pm-xc68 policy roles -> pm-is1a federation -> a third foreign-domain exemplar with an empty gap ledger. Depends on the SDK-complete milestone being reached first.\n\n## Explicit non-goals\nNo domain-specific policy in core. Exemplars are conformance vehicles, not products."
